for so long, then, your livelihood and your possessions they will devour,
as long as she holds to this purpose, whatever it is that now
in her breast the gods put.

For from her father I shall suffer evils, and other things a god
will give besides, since my mother will call down hateful Furies,
going out from the house;

But if to you it seems this thing more profitable and better
to be, one man’s livelihood unavenged to destroy,
then despoil it;

But when they came to the middle of the assembly, loud with many voices,
there, wheeling about, they shook their thick feathers,
and looked into the heads of all, and boded destruction;

for Odysseus will not be long away from his own dear ones,
but even now, somewhere, already being near,
he is planting murder and doom for all
these men;

for indeed for that man too, I say, all things have been fulfilled,
just as I told him, when up against Ilios were marching
the Argives, and with them went many-wiled Odysseus.

I said that, having suffered many evils, having lost all his companions,
unknown to everyone, in the twentieth year
he would come home;

if, knowing many things of old, with your words you beguile
a younger man and incite him to be harsh,
for himself it will be, first of all, the more grievous,
and yet he will be able to accomplish nothing, because of these men;

and his goods, moreover, will be wickedly devoured, nor ever equal
will they be again, for as long as she puts off the Achaeans
over her own marriage;
